Building BusyBox-RS:
====================

The BusyBox-RS build process provides multiple mechanisms: standard Make,
Cargo, or modern Nix Flakes.

Quick Start with Make:
----------------------

  make                # Builds the release binary via Cargo
  make test           # Runs test verification against the upstream test suite
  make install        # Installs binary and applet symlinks to $(PREFIX)

Quick Start with Nix Flakes:
----------------------------

  nix develop         # Drops into a fully provisioned development shell
  nix build           # Builds the static release package

Quick Start with Cargo:
-----------------------

  cargo build --release

  The compiled executable will be located at:
  target/release/busybox

Configuring Applets (Kconfig-style Feature Selection):
------------------------------------------------------

BusyBox-RS is optimized for size and modularity. Unused functionality can be
completely eliminated at compile time by selecting features in Cargo:

  # Build a minimal binary containing only specific applets:
  cargo build --release --no-default-features --features "echo,cat,ls,sh"

  # Or using Make targets:
  make defconfig      # Builds with all standard applets enabled
  make tiny           # Builds a minimal embedded profile

Installing Symlinks:
--------------------

To create the standard BusyBox symlink farm (pointing each applet command to the
single multi-call binary):

  make PREFIX=/usr/local/bin install

Or manually:

  for applet in $(./target/release/busybox --list); do
      ln -s busybox /usr/local/bin/"$applet"
  done
